Method:2 : Connect using username and pem (private key)
=======================================================

# create a user
sudo useradd -m -s /bin/bash viswa   # -m --> to create home directory, -s /bin/bash → set login shell


# create ssh keys in created user home directory (viswa)
cd /home/viswa
ssh-keygen

cat /home/viswa/.ssh/id_rsa.pub >> /home/viswa/.ssh/authorized_keys

chown -R viswa:viswa /home/viswa/.ssh

chmod 700 /home/viswa/.ssh
chmod 600 /home/viswa/.ssh/authorized_keys
chmod 600 /home/viswa/.ssh/id_rsa
chmod 644 /home/viswa/.ssh/id_rsa.pub


To connect:
===========
ssh -i chandra-nv.pem viswa@98.81.155.74


whoami   --> to verify the user



To disconnect:
==============
exit  or  ctrl+D   


To delete user
==============
sudo userdel john        #  --> user home directory won't be delete
sudo userdel -r john     # -r: it removes the user's home directory and its contents.


